		<h3 id="northernstar-dnn-network-label">Northern Star Scouting DNN Network</h3>
		<h4><a href="https://www.camptomahawk.org/" rel="external" target="_blank">Camp Tomahawk</a> (pictured)</h4>
		<p>This is more so a project about a shared DNN backend, not a single website: one DNN instance (inherited, along with EasyDNNNews and its Azure hosting) serves several Northern Star Scouting sites; Camp Tomahawk, <a href="https://www.northernstar.org/" rel="external" target="_blank">NorthernStar.org</a>, <a href="https://camp.northernstar.org/" rel="external" target="_blank">Camp.NorthernStar.org</a>, <a href="https://www.manypoint.org/" rel="external" target="_blank">ManyPoint.org</a>, <a href="https://www.explorebasecamp.org/" rel="external" target="_blank">ExploreBaseCamp.org</a>, and <a href="https://www.explorenow.org/" rel="external" target="_blank">ExploreNow.org</a>. I led a redesign across all six, on top of that inherited platform: a new shared skin, a rewrite of large parts of the CSS for accessibility, Google Tag Manager and Analytics, a Google Programmable Search Engine, automated redirects, security hardening, and a full reorganization of content network-wide.</p>
		<p>Camp Tomahawk (shown in this carousel) is the clearest example of how effective that redesign and reorganization were. Even without advertising or posting that it had happened, Camp Tomahawk saw:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>A 35% decrease in "easy questions" in phone calls and emails, such as "What is your address?" or "Where can I find the health form?"</li>
			<li>A 50% increase in impressions (5000) from search results</li>
			<li>A 20% increase in clicks from search results</li>
			<li>An 85% increase in the number of views of pages</li>
			<li>A 101% increase in sessions on the website</li>
			<li>An 8.2% decrease in bounce rate</li>
		</ul>
		<h4>Technologies</h4>
		<p>The network runs on the DNN content management system, which lets non-technical staff manage the sites without needing to work with HTML (or me). It uses EasyDNNNews to manage articles and has several display modules written with Bootstrap.</p>
